Local oracle fix: use-after-free in semantic reconciliation after a
view-model artboard swap.

Provenance:
  - Applies to pinned upstream rive-runtime 4ac7b32798da0482e441ef09304dc3b480ed3ee5
    (port-manifest.toml upstream_ref). No upstream commit exists for this fix;
    it is a local patch authored 2026-08-03 against the pinned oracle.
  - Symptom: rive_golden_runner{,_scripted} --side-channel flakily crashes
    (EXC_BAD_ACCESS) on corpus entries replace_view_model,
    data_binding_artboards_test, and stateful_source_switch — every asset that
    swaps artboards via ViewModelInstanceArtboard (type keys 598/599).
    Faulting stack: SemanticProvider::rootTransformAABB <-
    SemanticManager::reconcileBoundsForSubtree <- SemanticManager::drainDiff.
  - Root cause: NestedArtboard::updateArtboard destroys the outgoing
    ArtboardInstance (unique_ptr replacement in NestedArtboard::nest) while
    the shared SemanticManager still holds its semantic subtree. The
    boundary SemanticNode keeps a raw Artboard* (SemanticNode::
    boundaryArtboard) and SemanticData nodes keep raw Core* owners into the
    freed instance; the next drainDiff() reconciles bounds through freed
    memory. updateArtboard already detaches the focus tree
    (cleanupFocusTree) for the analogous reason but never detached the
    semantic tree.
  - Fix: mirror the focus-tree treatment. Detach the outgoing instance's
    semantic subtree (cleanupSemanticTree) before teardown, and register the
    swapped-in instance's subtree with the host tree's shared manager after
    mount, resolving the parent the same way Artboard::buildSemanticTree's
    nested-artboard propagation does.
  - Corpus-output neutral: none of the affected assets contain SemanticData
    objects (no semantic type keys in corpus.toml features), and boundary
    nodes are skipped during flattening, so detach/re-register changes no
    flattened snapshot and emits no diff records. Verified byte-identical
    side-channel recordings against the pre-fix non-crashing baseline.

diff --git a/src/nested_artboard.cpp b/src/nested_artboard.cpp
index 15fcbe6..c901f8b 100644
--- a/src/nested_artboard.cpp
+++ b/src/nested_artboard.cpp
@@ -12,6 +12,8 @@
 #include "rive/input/focusable.hpp"
 #include "rive/nested_animation.hpp"
 #include "rive/animation/nested_state_machine.hpp"
+#include "rive/semantic/semantic_data.hpp"
+#include "rive/semantic/semantic_manager.hpp"
 #include "rive/data_bind/data_bind_path.hpp"
 #include "rive/clip_result.hpp"
 #include "rive/text/text_input.hpp"
@@ -259,6 +261,16 @@ void NestedArtboard::updateArtboard(
     {
         outgoing->cleanupFocusTree();
     }
+    // Detach the outgoing instance's semantic subtree BEFORE teardown for the
+    // same reason: the shared SemanticManager retains raw back-pointers into
+    // the instance (the boundary node's Artboard*, SemanticData core owners).
+    // Destroying the instance while those nodes stay registered leaves the
+    // manager reconciling bounds through freed memory on the next
+    // drainDiff() (use-after-free in reconcileBoundsForSubtree).
+    if (outgoing != nullptr)
+    {
+        outgoing->cleanupSemanticTree();
+    }
     clearDataContext();
     clearNestedAnimations();
     m_boundNestedStateMachine = nullptr;
@@ -294,6 +306,26 @@ void NestedArtboard::updateArtboard(
         }
         referencedArtboard(artboardInstance.release());
 
+        // Register the swapped-in instance's semantic subtree with the host
+        // tree's shared SemanticManager (the counterpart of the
+        // cleanupSemanticTree() above). Without this, semantics inside the
+        // incoming artboard would stay unregistered until the next full
+        // buildSemanticTree() pass. Parent resolution mirrors
+        // Artboard::buildSemanticTree's nested-artboard propagation: closest
+        // enclosing semantic node, else the host artboard's boundary node.
+        auto* hostArtboard = this->artboard();
+        auto* semanticManager =
+            hostArtboard != nullptr ? hostArtboard->semanticManager() : nullptr;
+        if (semanticManager != nullptr && m_Instance != nullptr)
+        {
+            auto parentNode = SemanticData::findClosestSemanticNode(this);
+            if (parentNode == nullptr)
+            {
+                parentNode = hostArtboard->semanticBoundaryNode();
+            }
+            m_Instance->buildSemanticTree(semanticManager, parentNode);
+        }
+
         if (isStateful())
         {
             auto statefulChild = findStatefulChildVmi();
